    {
      "title": "Drone-hit tanker reaches Romania port, all 9 Indian seafarers safe",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/drone-hit-tanker-reaches-romania-port-all-9-indian-seafarers-safe-126101700781_1.html",
      "description": "A chemical tanker carrying nine Indian seafarers, which was hit by a drone at an anchorage off Romania earlier this week, has reached the Port of Constanta, with all crew members safe, the Indian mission in Bucharest said on Saturday.\nAmbassador Manoj Kumar Mohapatra spoke with Romanian search and rescue bodies, including SAR Romania and MRCC Constanta, as well as the chief security officer of the tanker YARA J, the Indian Embassy in Romania said in a post on X.\n\"It was confirmed that all nine Indian seafarers on board are safe and the vessel has arrived at the Port of Constanta,\" the embassy said.\nThe ambassador assured the crew of the Indian government's full support and assistance, it added.\nOn Friday, Shipping Minister Sarbananda Sonowal said YARA J was hit by a drone at Sulina Anchorage, Romania, on Wednesday.\nHe had also said that crude oil tanker MT ST 3, carrying 15 Indian seafarers, was struck by a projectile in the Strait of Hormuz on Friday.\nSonowal said all 24 Indian",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-17T14:13:24"
    }
